  "notes": [
    "All nine arms ran on the replacement L40S host with identical context/query identities; all candidate repeats were independently compared.",
    "Native estimator batch4 changes local arithmetic and passes BF16 comparison, but is not byte-identical to native1. Resident/process/graph predictions are byte-identical on every saved repeat.",
    "Parent and child allocator peaks are separate high-water counters, not a simultaneous whole-device peak. Device telemetry is sampled during actual prediction windows and includes driver/context/allocator overhead; sample maxima are lower bounds on physical peak.",
    "Child maximum RSS is lifetime high-water and can count shared pages; do not sum as unique host RAM.",
    "Warmup memory peaks include fit because reset occurs before fit and again after warmup. Graph worker capture durations overlap, so their sum is not capture wall time. Warmup wall time includes capture.",
    "No new graph is captured during measured prediction, as graph count remains4. Pretrained workload has no remainder batch; reduced-model tests cover remainder and retained-output lifetime.",
    "Initial native1 fit103.21s includes cold-start effects, unlike subsequent runs; fit speedup is not inferred. Resident1 third pass slowdown yields4.81% timing CV."
